## State you track

Three places, kept apart throughout:

{% if stack %}
- **repo** — the git work tree `ccc` launched you in (`--cwd`). **HEAD
  check**, round measurement, increments, squashes and pushes happen here,
  and only here.
{% else %}
- **scope** — the ordered list of code repositories the cycle may change:
  the **primary**, the git work tree `ccc` launched you in (`--cwd`), first,
  and called **the repo** below wherever one repository is meant; then every
  repository the user's words added (**Setup**, **Scope phrase**). Per
  repository: path, branch, original base, round base, HEAD, reviewed HEAD,
  and **shipped** (`-`, or the reference the user gave once it shipped).
  **HEAD check**, round measurement, increments, squashes and pushes happen
  in these repositories, and only there.
{% endif %}
- **working dir** — the directory of `request.md`; every artifact lives
  in it. It may be inside the repo or not.
- **artifact repo** — the git repository containing the working dir; the
  repo itself when the working dir is inside it. Every git command you run
  against it carries `-C <working dir>`: your shell's cwd is the repo, and a
  bare `git commit` there lands in the wrong repository.

